<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24984" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διακομ-ίξω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>carry over</i> or <i>across,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς τὴν νῆσον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.75
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέντε σταδίους δ. τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.31
				</span></i>
			; simply, <i>convey,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Merc.Cond.</u>
				27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLips.</u>
				34.5
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A.D.)</span>:—
				Med.
			, <i>carry over what is one's own,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. παῖδας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.89
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be carried over,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				136
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				905b
			</span></i>; <i>pass over, cross,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				3.30
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>recover, revive,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰ σιτίοισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Morb.</u>
					2.51
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
